INSERT INTO public.faqs (question, answer, category) VALUES
('How do I log in to QMS RISE?', 'Students log in using their registered institutional email address and password through the authentication system. The platform validates the user''s credentials and role before granting access. Session timeout, rate limiting, and account lockout are implemented to enhance security.', 'Authentication'),
('How do lecturers and staff log in?', 'Lecturers, Heads of Programme (HOPs), and the Dean authenticate using their registered staff credentials. After successful authentication, role-based access determines which modules and dashboards are available.', 'Authentication'),
('How does the system determine my user role?', 'After successful authentication, the system validates the user''s assigned role. Available interfaces and permissions are then restricted according to that role to ensure users access only authorised functions.', 'Authentication'),
('Why am I automatically logged out after being inactive?', 'QMS RISE automatically terminates inactive sessions after a predefined timeout period to reduce the risk of unauthorised access when devices are left unattended.', 'Authentication'),
('What is rate limiting?', 'Rate limiting restricts repeated authentication requests within a short period. This helps protect the platform against automated password guessing and excessive login attempts.', 'Authentication'),
('Why has my account been temporarily locked?', 'Accounts may be temporarily locked after multiple unsuccessful login attempts. This security measure reduces the likelihood of brute-force password attacks.', 'Authentication'),
('How do I change my password?', 'Users can change their password from the Profile module after successful authentication. Choosing a strong password is recommended to improve account security.', 'Authentication'),
('How are passwords protected?', 'Passwords are protected using SHA-256 hashing before storage. The system stores password hashes rather than plaintext passwords to improve credential security.', 'Authentication'),
('Can I view my own profile?', 'Yes. Authenticated users can access their own profile information and manage supported personal settings, including password changes and avatar management where available.', 'Authentication'),
('Why does the system display ''Invalid Credentials''?', 'This message indicates that the supplied authentication information does not match the registered account or the account cannot be validated. Verify your email address and password before trying again.', 'Authentication'),
('How do I log out safely?', 'Users should always log out using the Logout function before leaving the application, particularly when using shared or public computers.', 'Authentication'),
('Why can''t students access Dean features?', 'QMS RISE uses role-based access control. Student accounts cannot access administrative functions reserved for HOPs, lecturers, or the Dean.', 'Authentication'),
('Can I log in from multiple devices?', 'The system authenticates each session independently. Session behaviour depends on the current implementation and security configuration.', 'Authentication'),
('Can students register themselves?', 'Student registration depends on institutional configuration. Only authorised student records are permitted to create valid accounts.', 'Authentication'),
('Why does registration check official student records?', 'Registration validates users against authorised institutional records to prevent unauthorised account creation.', 'Authentication'),
('What happens during login?', 'The system validates the supplied credentials, verifies the assigned role, establishes a secure authenticated session, and loads the appropriate dashboard based on user permissions.', 'Authentication'),
('What is role-based access control?', 'Role-based access control ensures that every authenticated user only accesses modules and functions permitted for their assigned role.', 'Authentication'),
('What is a temporary password?', 'Temporary passwords may be issued when creating staff accounts or resetting credentials. Users should change them after their first successful login.', 'Authentication'),
('What should I do if I forget my password?', 'If you cannot remember your password, contact the authorised administrator or use the supported password reset process available within your deployment.', 'Authentication'),
('Why is session protection important?', 'Session protection reduces the risk of unauthorised account use by automatically ending inactive sessions and validating authenticated requests.', 'Authentication'),
('Can I upload a profile picture?', 'Yes. Users can upload and manage their profile avatar through the Profile module using integrated cloud storage.', 'Authentication'),
('Why do I receive a permission denied message?', 'This indicates that your current role does not have authorisation to access the requested function or module.', 'Authentication'),
('Why does QMS RISE use email-based authentication?', 'Email-based authentication provides a consistent institutional identity and simplifies account management across multiple user roles.', 'Authentication'),
('How are login credentials validated?', 'The authentication service validates submitted credentials against securely stored account information before granting access.', 'Authentication'),
('Are login activities recorded?', 'Authentication events may be recorded within system logs to support auditing, diagnostics, and security monitoring.', 'Authentication'),
('Is my login information protected?', 'Authentication information is protected through secure authentication practices and hashed password storage to improve overall platform security.', 'Authentication'),
('How does the system identify each user?', 'Each authenticated account is uniquely associated with its registered institutional identity and assigned system role.', 'Authentication'),
('Who should I contact if I cannot access my account?', 'Users should contact the authorised system administrator or designated academic support staff responsible for account administration.', 'Authentication'),
('Why is secure authentication important?', 'Secure authentication protects academic records, attendance, evaluations, documents, and administrative information from unauthorised access.', 'Authentication'),
('What security features are included in QMS RISE authentication?', 'QMS RISE authentication includes secure login, role validation, session timeout, rate limiting, account lockout, password hashing, and role-based access control to provide a secure user authentication framework.', 'Authentication'),
('How does QMS RISE protect against brute-force attacks?', 'QMS RISE implements rate limiting together with temporary account lockout after repeated unsuccessful login attempts. These controls significantly reduce the effectiveness of automated password guessing attacks while protecting legitimate user accounts.', 'Authentication'),
('How does QMS RISE protect authenticated sessions?', 'Authenticated sessions are managed securely through session validation and automatic timeout after inactivity. Users should always log out after using shared devices to minimise security risks.', 'Authentication'),
('What modules can students access after logging in?', 'Students can access modules assigned to the Student role, including their dashboard, QR attendance, lecturer evaluation, RISE points, Quiz Battle, AI Assistant, Chat, Complaints, Documents, Weekly Reports, and Profile.', 'Authentication'),
('What modules are available to lecturers?', 'Lecturers can access lecturer-specific functions such as attendance QR generation, evaluation reports relevant to their responsibilities, question generation, and other authorised academic management features.', 'Authentication'),
('What additional permissions does a Head of Programme have?', 'Heads of Programme have programme-specific management access, allowing them to monitor students, complaints, lecturer evaluations, attendance information, and programme analytics for programmes under their responsibility.', 'Authentication'),
('What permissions are available to the Dean?', 'The Dean has institution-wide administrative access to authorised dashboards including staff management, student management, analytics, evaluation reports, complaints, documents, and overall quality management functions.', 'Authentication'),
('Why should I avoid simple passwords?', 'Weak passwords increase the likelihood of unauthorised access. Users should choose passwords that are difficult to guess and avoid using personal information or common words.', 'Authentication'),
('Should I reuse my QMS RISE password on other websites?', 'No. Using unique passwords for different systems reduces the impact if another service experiences a security breach.', 'Authentication'),
('Can I log in using any web browser?', 'QMS RISE is designed as a web application and is intended to operate on modern web browsers that support current web technologies.', 'Authentication'),
('Will my work be lost if my session expires?', 'If your session expires because of inactivity, you may need to authenticate again before continuing. Saving work regularly is recommended when entering information.', 'Authentication'),
('Why does QMS RISE use institutional identities?', 'Institutional identities support accountability, auditing, role assignment, and secure access to academic information across the platform.', 'Authentication'),
('Why is user accountability important?', 'Individual authenticated accounts allow authorised actions to be traced to specific users, supporting transparency and institutional governance.', 'Authentication'),
('Why are administrator functions hidden from students?', 'Administrative functions are restricted to authorised roles to protect sensitive institutional information and prevent unauthorised modifications.', 'Authentication'),
('Can I update my profile picture at any time?', 'Yes. Users can update their avatar through the Profile module, subject to the storage capabilities provided by the implemented system.', 'Authentication'),
('When should I change my password?', 'Users should change their password whenever they suspect it may have been compromised or when instructed by institutional policy.', 'Authentication'),
('What should I check before reporting a login problem?', 'Verify that your registered email address is correct, your password is accurate, and your account has not been temporarily locked because of repeated failed login attempts.', 'Authentication'),
('Should I email my password to support staff?', 'No. Legitimate administrators should never ask for your password. Passwords should remain confidential at all times.', 'Authentication'),
('Who provides authentication support?', 'Authentication issues should be handled by authorised system administrators or designated university support personnel responsible for account management.', 'Authentication'),
('Is it safe to use QMS RISE on a public computer?', 'Yes, provided you always log out completely after use and avoid allowing browsers to save your password on shared devices.', 'Authentication'),
('What components make up the authentication system?', 'The authentication system combines secure login, Supabase Authentication, password hashing, role validation, session timeout, rate limiting, and account lockout.', 'Authentication'),
('When is my role verified?', 'User roles are verified immediately after successful authentication before dashboards and protected modules are loaded.', 'Authentication'),
('Can temporary accounts be created?', 'Temporary credentials may be issued during account provisioning or password reset, after which users should update their password.', 'Authentication'),
('Can administrators monitor authentication activity?', 'Authentication events may be recorded through audit logging mechanisms to support troubleshooting, security monitoring, and compliance activities.', 'Authentication'),
('Why is secure login required before accessing dashboards?', 'Dashboards contain protected academic and administrative information that should only be available to authenticated and authorised users.', 'Authentication'),
('Why is identity verification important?', 'Identity verification ensures that users access only their authorised information while protecting institutional data from unauthorised access.', 'Authentication'),
('How does authentication improve data integrity?', 'Restricting access to authenticated users helps maintain the integrity of attendance, evaluations, reports, and academic records.', 'Authentication'),
('How do I recover access to my account?', 'If you cannot access your account, contact the authorised administrator responsible for user account management to verify your identity and initiate recovery procedures.', 'Authentication'),
('What security principles guide the authentication system?', 'The implemented authentication framework emphasises confidentiality, integrity, accountability, role-based access control, and secure credential management.', 'Authentication'),
('Why is authentication considered a core module?', 'Authentication is the foundation of QMS RISE because every protected function—including attendance, evaluations, analytics, reports, and management—depends on verified user identity and authorised access.', 'Authentication'),
('What is included in the QMS RISE authentication framework?', 'The framework includes secure authentication through Supabase Authentication, SHA-256 password protection, session timeout, rate limiting, account lockout, role validation, profile management, and role-based access control for all supported user roles.', 'Authentication'),
('I am sure my password is correct, but I still cannot log in. What should I do?', 'Verify that you are using your registered institutional email address, check that Caps Lock is not enabled, and ensure your account has not been temporarily locked because of repeated failed login attempts. If the issue persists, contact the authorised system administrator to verify your account status.', 'Authentication'),
('How long does an account remain locked after repeated failed logins?', 'QMS RISE temporarily locks accounts after repeated unsuccessful authentication attempts. The lock duration depends on the deployed security configuration. If immediate access is required, contact an authorised administrator.', 'Authentication'),
('Can browser cache cause login problems?', 'Yes. Cached authentication data or expired browser sessions may occasionally interfere with authentication. Refreshing the browser or signing in again usually resolves the issue.', 'Authentication'),
('What should I do before leaving a shared computer?', 'Always log out using the Logout function and close the browser to prevent unauthorised access to your account.', 'Authentication'),
('What should I do if I suspect someone has accessed my account?', 'Immediately change your password if possible and notify the authorised system administrator so appropriate security checks can be performed.', 'Authentication'),
('Who creates user accounts in QMS RISE?', 'User accounts are created and managed through authorised administrative processes to ensure that only legitimate institutional users receive system access.', 'Authentication'),
('Who assigns user roles?', 'User roles are assigned by authorised administrators according to institutional responsibilities. These roles determine accessible dashboards and permitted functions.', 'Authentication'),
('Why does QMS RISE restrict user permissions?', 'The platform follows role-based access control so users receive only the permissions necessary for their responsibilities, reducing security risks.', 'Authentication'),
('Why are authentication events important for auditing?', 'Authentication events provide accountability by recording significant access activities, supporting institutional governance, troubleshooting, and security investigations.', 'Authentication'),
('Why did my session expire while I was using the system?', 'Sessions may expire after prolonged inactivity. This security feature reduces the likelihood of unauthorised access if a device is left unattended.', 'Authentication'),
('How often should I change my password?', 'Users should update their password whenever compromise is suspected or according to institutional security policies.', 'Authentication'),
('What characteristics should a secure password have?', 'A secure password should be difficult to guess, unique to QMS RISE, and not based on personal information or common words.', 'Authentication'),
('Who can reset my password?', 'Password resets are performed through authorised administrative procedures or the supported password reset process configured for your deployment.', 'Authentication'),
('Can I allow my friend to log in using my account?', 'No. Every account represents one authorised institutional user. Sharing credentials compromises accountability and system security.', 'Authentication'),
('Can a student''s role be changed to lecturer?', 'Role changes require administrative modification of authorised account records. Users cannot change their own role.', 'Authentication'),
('Can an account be disabled?', 'Yes. Administrators may deactivate accounts when users leave the institution or no longer require access.', 'Authentication'),
('Why is confidentiality important in authentication?', 'Authentication protects confidential academic records, reports, attendance information, and administrative data from unauthorised access.', 'Authentication'),
('Why was Supabase Authentication selected?', 'Supabase Authentication provides secure user authentication, session management, and integration suitable for the implemented QMS RISE architecture.', 'Authentication'),
('Why does QMS RISE use SHA-256 password hashing?', 'Password hashing ensures that plaintext passwords are never stored directly, reducing exposure if stored authentication data is compromised.', 'Authentication'),
('How is role-based access control implemented?', 'After successful authentication, the user''s assigned role determines which modules, dashboards, and operations are available throughout the application.', 'Authentication'),
('Can the AI Assistant help with login problems?', 'The AI Assistant can explain authentication procedures, common troubleshooting steps, and direct users to appropriate support processes. It cannot bypass authentication or reveal passwords.', 'Authentication'),
('Why do I receive ''Permission Denied'' after logging in?', 'Successful authentication does not automatically grant access to every feature. Access depends on your assigned role and authorised permissions.', 'Authentication'),
('What should I do after receiving a temporary password?', 'Log in using the temporary password and immediately change it through the Profile module to improve account security.', 'Authentication'),
('How should suspected unauthorised access be handled?', 'Administrators should investigate authentication logs, verify user identity, reset credentials if necessary, and review affected accounts according to institutional procedures.', 'Authentication'),
('How does authentication support institutional compliance?', 'Authentication establishes verified user identity, role accountability, and controlled access, supporting governance and quality assurance activities.', 'Authentication'),
('Why should repeated failed logins be avoided?', 'Repeated failures may trigger temporary account lockout designed to protect user accounts from automated attacks.', 'Authentication'),
('What security layers are included in authentication?', 'Authentication combines secure login, password hashing, role validation, session timeout, account lockout, and rate limiting into a layered security model.', 'Authentication'),
('When should I contact technical support?', 'Contact support when authentication problems cannot be resolved using normal troubleshooting steps or when account verification is required.', 'Authentication'),
('What are the most important authentication security practices?', 'Use a strong unique password, never share credentials, always log out from shared devices, and report suspicious activity immediately.', 'Authentication'),
('What is the primary purpose of the authentication module?', 'The authentication module ensures that only verified and authorised users can securely access QMS RISE according to their assigned institutional role while protecting academic and administrative information.', 'Authentication'),
('What is the Student Dashboard?', 'The Student Dashboard is the main landing page after a student logs into QMS RISE. It provides quick access to attendance, RISE points, lecturer evaluations, Quiz Battle Arena, AI Assistant, chat, complaints, documents, weekly reports, profile management, and other authorised student services.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('What can I access from the Student Dashboard?', 'Students can access QR Attendance, Lecturer Evaluation, RISE Dashboard, Quiz Battle Arena, AI Assistant, Student Chat, Complaint System, Document Management, Weekly Reports, Profile, and other authorised modules available to the Student role.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('What information is displayed on the Student Dashboard?', 'The dashboard provides an overview of the student''s activities and serves as a central navigation point to implemented academic engagement features.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Why can I only see student features?', 'QMS RISE uses role-based access control. Students only see modules that are authorised for the Student role.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Is the Student Dashboard personalised?', 'Yes. The dashboard presents information associated with the authenticated student account and authorised student services.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('When can I access my Student Dashboard?', 'The dashboard becomes available immediately after successful authentication using a valid student account.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Is my Student Dashboard private?', 'Yes. Only authenticated users can access their own dashboard. Student information is protected through role-based access control.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Why does the dashboard provide shortcuts?', 'Quick-access cards reduce navigation time by allowing students to open frequently used modules directly from the dashboard.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Why was my dashboard closed automatically?', 'If your authenticated session expires because of inactivity, you must log in again before accessing the dashboard.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('What is the purpose of the Student Dashboard?', 'The Student Dashboard centralises access to all student-related functions within QMS RISE and provides a single entry point for academic engagement activities.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('What is the RISE Dashboard?', 'The RISE Dashboard displays a student''s engagement progress within the Recognition for Involvement and Skills Enhancement (RISE) framework, including accumulated points, category progress, tier status, and leaderboard information where applicable.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Where can I see my RISE points?', 'Students can view their accumulated RISE points through the RISE Dashboard after logging into QMS RISE.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('How many RISE categories are implemented?', 'QMS RISE v7 implements eight RISE categories with equal contribution weighting toward the overall RISE score.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('How are RISE categories weighted?', 'Each of the eight RISE categories contributes equally at 12.5% toward the overall RISE score according to the implemented gamification framework.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Can I see my current RISE tier?', 'Yes. The RISE Dashboard displays the student''s current tier based on the implemented gamification calculations.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Can I view the leaderboard?', 'Yes. Students can access the leaderboard to compare their RISE performance with other eligible students.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Does the dashboard display progress?', 'Yes. The RISE Dashboard includes progress indicators that help students monitor their engagement achievements.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Can I view progress for each RISE category?', 'Yes. Students can monitor their accumulated progress across the implemented RISE categories through the dashboard.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Why is the RISE Dashboard important?', 'The dashboard encourages continuous participation by allowing students to monitor engagement progress and identify opportunities for further involvement.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('What information does the RISE Dashboard summarise?', 'The dashboard summarises the student''s engagement achievements, points, category progress, and tier information.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Will the Student Dashboard notify me about important activities?', 'The dashboard serves as the central location for accessing student services. Notifications available depend on the implemented modules and authorised functionality.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Can I access my profile from the dashboard?', 'Yes. Students can open the Profile module directly from the Student Dashboard.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Can I access Weekly Reports from the dashboard?', 'Yes. Weekly Reports are available through the Student Dashboard as part of the implemented reporting features.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Can I open the AI Assistant from the dashboard?', 'Yes. The AI Assistant is directly accessible from the Student Dashboard for supported questions about QMS RISE.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Can I launch Quiz Battle Arena from the dashboard?', 'Yes. Students can access Quiz Battle Arena directly from the Student Dashboard.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Can I submit complaints from the dashboard?', 'Yes. Students can open the Complaint System directly from the Student Dashboard.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Can I access my documents from the dashboard?', 'Yes. The Document Management module is accessible through the Student Dashboard for authorised document operations.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Can I message my Head of Programme from the dashboard?', 'Yes. Students can access the Student Chat module from the dashboard to communicate with their authorised Head of Programme.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Can I submit lecturer evaluations from the Student Dashboard?', 'Yes. The Lecturer Evaluation module is directly accessible from the Student Dashboard for authorised evaluation submissions.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Can I record attendance from the Student Dashboard?', 'Yes. Students can access the QR Attendance scanner directly from the Student Dashboard to record attendance for authorised class sessions.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('What do I see immediately after logging in?', 'After successful authentication, students are presented with the Student Dashboard, which serves as the central navigation hub for all authorised student services, including attendance, RISE, evaluations, Quiz Battle, AI Assistant, chat, complaints, documents, reports, and profile management.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Why are dashboard modules displayed as cards?', 'Dashboard cards provide quick visual navigation to commonly used modules, reducing the number of clicks required to access student services.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Does the Student Dashboard work on different screen sizes?', 'Yes. QMS RISE v7 uses a responsive interface so the dashboard can adapt to different screen sizes while maintaining usability.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Why does the dashboard use a glassmorphism design?', 'The implemented UI adopts a glassmorphism-inspired design to provide a modern, visually appealing interface while maintaining readability and usability.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('What is the neural canvas background?', 'The neural canvas is part of the implemented visual design theme that enhances the overall appearance of QMS RISE without affecting system functionality.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('What is my overall RISE score?', 'Your overall RISE score is calculated using the implemented gamification framework, where eight categories contribute equally to your final engagement score.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Why should I participate in different RISE categories?', 'Each implemented category contributes equally to the overall RISE score. Balanced participation across categories helps maximise overall performance.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Why did my points stop increasing in one category?', 'QMS RISE implements category caps within the gamification framework. Once a category reaches its configured maximum contribution, additional activities in that category may not increase the weighted score further.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('How is my leaderboard position determined?', 'Leaderboard rankings are determined using the implemented RISE scoring framework based on accumulated eligible engagement points.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('How can I monitor my engagement progress?', 'Students can monitor their accumulated RISE points, category progress, and tier information through the RISE Dashboard.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('How do I update dashboard information?', 'Dashboard information is refreshed according to the application''s current data retrieval process. Reloading the page will display the latest available information.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('How quickly can I access attendance?', 'The Student Dashboard provides direct access to the QR Attendance scanner to simplify attendance recording.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Why is Lecturer Evaluation displayed prominently?', 'Lecturer Evaluation is a core student quality assurance activity and is therefore directly accessible from the dashboard.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Why is Quiz Battle available from the dashboard?', 'Quiz Battle Arena is integrated into the student dashboard to encourage continuous engagement through gamified learning.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Why is the AI Assistant easily accessible?', 'The AI Assistant is intended to provide immediate support for questions related to QMS RISE and student services.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Can I manage documents directly from the dashboard?', 'Yes. Students can access the Document Management module from the dashboard to upload, preview, download, or delete authorised documents.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Why is Chat available on the dashboard?', 'The integrated Student Chat allows direct communication with the authorised Head of Programme without leaving the platform.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('How do I submit a complaint from the dashboard?', 'Students can open the Complaint System directly from the dashboard and submit authorised complaints for review.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('What are Weekly Reports?', 'Weekly Reports provide an automated summary of implemented engagement information, including the Top 5 leaderboard.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Can I change my profile from the dashboard?', 'Yes. The dashboard provides access to the Profile module for supported profile management functions.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Why is the dashboard considered the central hub?', 'The Student Dashboard brings together all implemented student services into a single interface, reducing navigation complexity.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Why are some modules not visible?', 'Only modules authorised for the Student role are displayed. Administrative features remain restricted to authorised staff roles.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Can I customise which modules appear?', 'Module visibility depends on the implemented system configuration and authorised permissions. Personal customisation of dashboard modules is not documented as an implemented feature.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Why does the dashboard load quickly?', 'The dashboard is designed to provide efficient access to frequently used student services while presenting essential information in a single location.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Can another student view my dashboard?', 'No. Dashboard information is available only after successful authentication and is associated with the authenticated student account.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Can I return to the dashboard from other modules?', 'Yes. The dashboard serves as the primary navigation hub, allowing students to move efficiently between implemented modules.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Why is the dashboard organised into modules?', 'Organising features into modules improves usability by grouping related functions together and making navigation more intuitive.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('How does the Student Dashboard improve productivity?', 'The dashboard reduces navigation time by providing centralised access to the most frequently used academic engagement functions.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('How are different student services connected?', 'Implemented modules are accessible through the Student Dashboard, allowing students to move between authorised services without separate logins.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('What is the overall purpose of the Student Dashboard?', 'The Student Dashboard serves as the central gateway to all implemented student functions, enabling secure, efficient, and organised access to academic engagement services within QMS RISE.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('What are the dashboard overview cards?', 'Dashboard overview cards provide quick access to frequently used student modules such as QR Attendance, Lecturer Evaluation, RISE Dashboard, Quiz Battle Arena, AI Assistant, Chat, Complaints, Documents, Weekly Reports, and Profile management.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Why are all major features accessible from one dashboard?', 'The Student Dashboard centralises commonly used academic engagement features to minimise navigation time and improve the overall user experience.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Does every student see the same dashboard?', 'Students access the same core dashboard structure, but available functions depend on their authorised permissions and system configuration.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Why is the Student Dashboard the first page after login?', 'It serves as the primary workspace where students can immediately access their authorised academic engagement services.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Can I access the dashboard from different devices?', 'The responsive interface is designed to adapt to different screen sizes while maintaining usability.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Can I navigate directly between modules?', 'Yes. Students can move directly between authorised modules using the dashboard navigation without needing to authenticate again during an active session.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('What are quick actions?', 'Quick actions are shortcuts that allow students to open frequently used modules directly from the dashboard.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('How does the dashboard improve usability?', 'The dashboard groups related student services into organised sections, allowing users to locate functions quickly and efficiently.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Why can''t I access lecturer menus?', 'Lecturer and administrative modules are protected using role-based access control and are unavailable to student accounts.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Can I always return to the home dashboard?', 'Yes. The Student Dashboard serves as the central navigation point throughout the application.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('How can I monitor my overall engagement?', 'Students can monitor their engagement through the RISE Dashboard, which displays accumulated points, category progress, and tier information.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('How does QMS RISE encourage participation?', 'The platform recognises student involvement through the implemented RISE gamification framework, encouraging participation across multiple engagement categories.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Why should I participate in different activities?', 'The implemented scoring framework gives equal weighting to eight RISE categories, encouraging balanced participation instead of focusing on only one activity type.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Why is there a leaderboard?', 'The leaderboard promotes healthy competition by allowing eligible students to compare their engagement performance.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Does the leaderboard affect my grades?', 'No. The implemented documentation describes the leaderboard as part of the RISE engagement framework and not as an academic grading component.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Can I access attendance records from the dashboard?', 'Students can access the QR Attendance module through the dashboard to participate in authorised attendance recording.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Where do I submit lecturer evaluations?', 'Lecturer evaluations are submitted through the Lecturer Evaluation module, which is accessible from the Student Dashboard.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Can I immediately start Quiz Battle?', 'Students can open the Quiz Battle Arena from the dashboard and participate according to the implemented quiz rules.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('When should I use the AI Assistant?', 'Students can use the AI Assistant for questions related to supported QMS RISE functions and academic engagement processes.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('How do I communicate with my Head of Programme?', 'Students can use the integrated Student Chat module to communicate with their authorised Head of Programme.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Where can I report an issue?', 'Students can submit issues through the Complaint System available from the Student Dashboard.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Can I manage academic documents?', 'Students can access the Document Management module to perform authorised document operations such as upload, preview, download, and deletion.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('What information is included in Weekly Reports?', 'Weekly Reports provide an automated summary of implemented engagement information together with the Top 5 leaderboard.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Can I manage my personal profile?', 'Yes. Students can access the Profile module to manage supported account settings, including password changes and avatar management.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Can another student access my dashboard?', 'No. Dashboard information is protected by authentication and role-based access control and is available only to the authenticated user.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Why is every module connected through the dashboard?', 'A centralised dashboard simplifies navigation and provides a consistent user experience across implemented student services.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Are all student modules integrated?', 'Yes. Implemented student modules are accessible through the Student Dashboard, providing a unified user experience.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('How does the dashboard improve efficiency?', 'Centralising access to major student functions reduces navigation time and helps students complete routine academic tasks more efficiently.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Why is the Student Dashboard different from the Dean Dashboard?', 'Each dashboard is designed for a specific user role. Students access engagement functions, while administrative dashboards provide management and analytics capabilities.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('What is the overall objective of the Student Dashboard?', 'The Student Dashboard provides secure, organised, and efficient access to all implemented student engagement services within QMS RISE through a single authenticated interface.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Why haven''t my RISE points updated yet?', 'RISE points are updated after eligible activities have been successfully recorded according to the implemented scoring rules. If an activity has not yet been processed or verified, the updated score may not appear immediately.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('How are my RISE points calculated?', 'RISE points are calculated according to the implemented gamification framework, where eligible activities contribute toward eight equally weighted categories. Category caps are applied where configured.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('I think my RISE points are incorrect. What should I do?', 'Review the activities that have been successfully recorded. If you believe an eligible activity has not been reflected correctly, contact the authorised administrator or Head of Programme for verification.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Why did my leaderboard ranking change?', 'Leaderboard rankings automatically change as eligible engagement activities are recorded for all participating students.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Why did my ranking decrease even though I earned points?', 'Your ranking depends on comparative performance. Other students may also have earned additional eligible RISE points.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Is the leaderboard updated automatically?', 'The leaderboard reflects the latest available implemented RISE data after eligible activities have been processed.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Where can I find the QR attendance scanner?', 'The QR Attendance scanner can be accessed directly from the Student Dashboard.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Why does attendance require my location?', 'The implemented attendance system validates that students are within the authorised GPS radius before attendance can be successfully recorded.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Why can''t I scan the QR code anymore?', 'Attendance QR codes are generated with limited validity. If the QR code has expired, students must obtain the current QR code generated by the lecturer.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Why can''t I scan attendance twice?', 'Duplicate attendance submissions are prevented to ensure attendance integrity.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('What happens if I am outside the allowed GPS radius?', 'Attendance validation will not be successful if your location falls outside the implemented GPS validation radius.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('How do I earn the weekly attendance bonus?', 'Students who satisfy the implemented weekly attendance requirement become eligible for the configured attendance bonus.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('How is the semester attendance bonus awarded?', 'Students who satisfy the implemented semester attendance requirement receive the configured semester attendance bonus.', 'Student Dashboard'),
('Can I monitor my attendance bonus progress?', 'Attendance-related progress can be monitored through the implemented attendance and RISE features available to students.', 'Student Dashboard'),
